Source: syncthing-socket
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tobias Mueller <tobias.mueller@sitasys.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/muelli/syncthing-socket
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: syncthing-socket
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: netcat-like tunnel over the Syncthing relay network
 syncthing-socket connects two hosts that cannot accept inbound connections, by
 meeting on the public Syncthing relay network and Syncthing's global discovery.
 Peers are identified by Syncthing Device IDs, traffic is TLS 1.3 end to end, and
 an ICE/WebRTC upgrade replaces the relay with a direct peer-to-peer link when the
 network allows it.
 .
 It offers a raw stdin/stdout pipe, a PTY shell, single-command execution, port
 forwarding and reverse forwarding, and a SOCKS5 proxy.

Package: syncthing-socket-luks-initramfs
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         syncthing-socket,
         cryptsetup-initramfs,
         initramfs-tools | initramfs-tools-core,
         ca-certificates
Recommends: dropbear-initramfs, qrencode
Description: unlock a LUKS root volume over the Syncthing relay network
 Fetches a LUKS passphrase during early boot over the Syncthing relay network, so
 a machine that cannot accept inbound connections can still be unlocked remotely.
 The booting machine only makes outbound connections; the key holder pipes the
 passphrase into "syncthing-socket server" on demand.
 .
 This package installs an initramfs-tools hook, local-top and local-bottom scripts,
 and the helpers to store the configuration in the LUKS2 header. It does not install
 a cryptsetup keyscript: it races cryptsetup's own prompt through the passfifo, so
 console entry and cryptroot-unlock keep working. It is separate from the
 syncthing-socket package because it rewrites your boot path and is only useful on
 systems using initramfs-tools.
 .
 Installing it is not enough on its own: the unlock configuration has to be stored
 in the LUKS2 header with syncthing-luks-bind and the initramfs rebuilt. /etc/crypttab
 needs no changes. See
 /usr/share/doc/syncthing-socket-luks-initramfs/README.md.
